          "jcr:created": "Tue Sep 17 2024 20:26:29 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-8em\"><b>References</b></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><span class=\"fontsize-8em\">1. World Health Organization. (2025, December 6). Most countries make progress towards universal health coverage, but major challenges remain, WHO–World Bank report finds [News release]. <a href=\"https://www.who.int/news/item/06-12-2025-most-countries-make-progress-towards-universal-health-coverage-but-major-challenges-remain-who-world-bank-report-finds\">https://www.who.int/news/item/06-12-2025-most-countries-make-progress-towards-universal-health-coverage-but-major-challenges-remain-who-world-bank-report-finds</a><br>\n 2. Data on file with Operation Smile.<br>\n 3. American Red Cross. ‘Importance of the Blood Supply.’ Accessed 10 October 2024 via <a href=\"https://www.redcrossblood.org/donate-blood/how-to-donate/how-blood-donations-help/blood-needs-blood-supply.html\">https://www.redcrossblood.org/donate-blood/how-to-donate/how-blood-donations-help/blood-needs-blood-supply.html</a> <br>\n 4. Global Surgery 2030: evidence and solutions for achieving health, welfare, and economic development – The Lancet accessed 10 October 2024 via <a href=\"https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(15)60160-X/fulltext\">https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(15)60160-X/fulltext</a><br>\n 5. Data on file with Project C.U.R.E.</span><br>\n</p>\n",
